{# Per-render-block template for AGENTS.md.

   Context variables:
     block:    the eawf.profiles.models.RenderBlock currently being rendered.
     composed: the full ComposedProfile (so future templates can reach for
               provenance / sibling render_blocks if needed).

   A block carries its body in exactly one of two shapes (the RenderBlock
   model-validator enforces the XOR):

   - Prose: ``block.body_template`` is non-empty markdown emitted verbatim.
     That gives profile authors complete control over their block's surface
     text without forcing them to think about jinja escaping.
   - Structured: the ``rationale`` / ``mechanism`` / ``verification`` triad is
     populated and ``body_template`` is empty. We emit a fixed
     Rationale / Mechanism / Verification sub-heading layout from the triad so
     authors who want the canonical three-part rule shape do not hand-format
     markdown. ``block.is_structured`` is ``True`` exactly in this case.

   When a future profile body needs jinja substitution inside body_template,
   replace the prose line below with
   `{{ block.body_template | render_jinja(composed) }}` or similar — the
   renderer routes both the block and the composed profile into this template's
   context, so adding a richer expansion is non-breaking.

   The trailing newline matters: replace_region strips one boundary newline at
   each end of the body, so the literal output below round-trips cleanly. #}
{%- if block.is_structured -%}
### Rationale

{{ block.rationale }}

### Mechanism

{{ block.mechanism }}

### Verification

{{ block.verification }}
{%- else -%}
{{- block.body_template -}}
{%- endif -%}
